    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>Wondrous Item, Artifact (Requires Attunement)</em></p><p>Written by the archmage Iggwilv, this treatise maps the layers and inhabitants of the Abyss and is widely held to be the most thorough and blasphemous work of demonology in the multiverse. It records both the oldest and the latest profanities of the Abyss and its demons. Demons have tried to censor it, tearing whole sections from its spine, yet its main chapters remain and keep revealing demonic secrets. Behind its lines of script churns a hidden piece of the Abyss itself, which keeps the book up to date however many pages are removed—and which longs to be more than a reference.</p><p><strong>Abyssal Lore.</strong> You can consult the <em>Demonomicon</em> whenever you make an Intelligence check to learn about demons or a Wisdom (Survival) check related to the Abyss; when you do, you have Advantage on the check.</p><p><strong>Containment.</strong> The first ten pages of the <em>Demonomicon</em> are blank. As a Magic action while holding the book, you can target a Fiend you can see that is trapped within the area of a @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplMagicCircl]{Magic Circle} spell. The Fiend must succeed on a DC 20 Charisma saving throw with Disadvantage or be trapped in one of the blank pages, which fills with writing detailing the creature’s widely known name and depravities. Once used, this action can’t be used again until the next dawn.</p><p>When you finish a Long Rest, if you and the book are on the same plane of existence, one creature trapped in it can try to possess you. You make a DC 20 Charisma saving throw. On a failed save, the creature possesses you and controls you like a puppet; as a Magic action, it can release you and appear in the unoccupied space closest to you. On a successful save, that Fiend can’t try to possess you again for 7 days (though another Fiend trapped in the book certainly can).</p><p>When the tome is found, 1d4 Fiends—usually an assortment of demons—occupy its pages.</p><p><strong>Ensnarement.</strong> While carrying the book, whenever you cast @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplMagicCircl]{Magic Circle} naming only Fiends or cast @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplPlanarBind]{Planar Binding} targeting a Fiend, the spell is cast at level 9, whatever spell slot you used, if any, and the Fiend has Disadvantage on its saving throw against it.</p><p><strong>Fiendish Scourging.</strong> While carrying the book, when you make a damage roll for a spell you cast against a Fiend, you use the maximum possible result instead of rolling.</p><p><strong>Random Properties.</strong> The Artifact has the following random properties (see “Artifacts”):</p><ul><li><p>2 minor beneficial properties</p></li><li><p>1 minor detrimental property</p></li><li><p>1 major detrimental property</p></li></ul><p><strong>Spells.</strong> The book has 8 charges and regains 1d8 expended charges daily at dawn. While holding it, you can take a Magic action to cast one of the spells on the following table (save DC 20), expending the number of charges it shows.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Spell</th><th>Charge Cost</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplMagicCircl]{Magic Circle}</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplMagicJar00]{Magic Jar}</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplPlanarAlly]{Planar Ally}</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplPlanarBind]{Planar Binding}</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplPlaneShift]{Plane Shift}</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>Summon Fiend</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplTashasHide]{Hideous Laughter}</td><td>0</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Destroying the Demonomicon.</strong> To destroy the book, six different demon lords must each tear out a sixth of its pages. If they do, the pages reappear after 24 hours. Before then, anyone who opens the remaining binding is transported to a nascent layer of the Abyss hidden within the book. At the heart of this deadly, semisentient domain lies a long-lost Artifact, <em>Fraz-Urb’luu’s Staff</em>. If the staff is dragged out of the pocket plane, the tome becomes a mundane, out-of-date copy of the <em>Tome of Zyx</em>, the work on which the <em>Demonomicon</em> was founded, and it can be destroyed like any ordinary book. The demon lord Fraz-Urb’luu knows the instant the staff emerges.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-cIVO36yFH4BczYVs\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>Les propriétés aléatoires d’artefact sont à ajouter par le MJ. <em>Summon Fiend</em> n’existe pas dans dnd5e : son activité <em>Cast</em> est vide, déposez-y le sort si vous l’avez. Le Désavantage de <em>Containment</em>, <em>Abyssal Lore</em>, <em>Ensnarement</em> et <em>Fiendish Scourging</em> sont à appliquer à la main.</p></section>",
      "chat": ""
    },
